ument exists that answers the execution engine question\n  with a single selected option and records the decision rationale.\n- Each option is evaluated against named criteria: ability to launch\n  evaluations against KServe endpoints and Llama Stack distributions, support\n  for standard and custom benchmark tasks, ability to serve the Llama Stack\n  eval provider API, and result persistence hooks.\n- The bounded outcomes are enumerated (extend LMEvalJob as single execution\n  path vs new evaluation service) so the conditional downstream plan can be\n  resolved.\n- Downstream impact on the Dashboard integration, the Data Science Pipelines\n  evaluation step, and the Llama Stack eval provider is stated for the\n  selected option.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): launching evaluations of served models — gated by this\n  investigation's outcome.\n- HLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack eval provider API backed by the platform evaluation\n  service — gated by this investigation's outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47092,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab93c870253e5ee8","agent_id":"a1f24615f07c0d279","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"3a8c50ec-b9fd-447b-9389-811f84ee1d49","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:13:54.067Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
