{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a05a315a-c7ed-44e1-b9cf-2fb1ff93f702","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1b1c7409a56960d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-twq9v194/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E009.md","content":"# Extend LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n\n## Description\n\nConditional plan branch A — applies if the execution engine architecture\ninvestigation recommends building on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob as the single\nexecution path. This epic extends the LMEvalJob capability so users can launch\nan evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama\nStack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite, run custom evaluation\ntasks through the same flow, and have results — including cost/duration\nmetadata — persisted and linked to the Model Registry version of the evaluated\nmodel.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the LMEvalJob-based execution path so an evaluation can be launched\n  against a model served on the platform (KServe InferenceService endpoint or\n  Llama Stack distribution) with a selected benchmark suite from the standard\n  catalog.\n- Support custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) through\n  the same launch flow as standard suites.\n- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the\n  evaluated model's version, in the canonical result schema, including the\n  link to the evaluated model version.\n- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the same\n  result record for capacity planning.\n- Preserve existing LMEvalJob behavior for current users of the Tech Preview\n  capability.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform against a\n  selected benchmark suite, and the evaluation executes via the LMEvalJob\n  path.\n- Custom evaluation tasks with user-defined datasets and metrics run through\n  the same flow as standard suites.\n- On completion, results are persisted to Model Registry custom properties on\n  the evaluated model version, conforming to the canonical result schema.\n- Each evaluation run records tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU time in the\n  result record.\n- Existing LMEvalJob usage (pre-extension) continues to function.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the\n  platform against a selected benchmark suite.\n- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks and run them through\n  the same flow.\n- HLR-8 (P2): evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata for capacity\n  planning (same result record and persistence surface as HLR-3 — bundled, not\n  split).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51736,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab93c870253e5ee8","agent_id":"a1f24615f07c0d279","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"41824321-0cc1-4650-ab3f-ee9834041dd8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:15:20.201Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
