{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a05a315a-c7ed-44e1-b9cf-2fb1ff93f702","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6acdb4ecb44636","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-twq9v194/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E009.md","content":"# New evaluation service for execution and the eval provider API\n\n## Description\n\nConditional plan branch B — applies if the execution engine architecture\ninvestigation recommends a new evaluation service. This epic builds that\nservice under the TrustyAI component (the platform's model-quality component):\nit exposes the platform's evaluation launch surface, executes evaluations of\nmodels served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution)\nagainst selected benchmark suites, supports custom evaluation tasks, persists\nresults — including cost/duration metadata — linked to the Model Registry\nversion of the evaluated model, and serves the API surface that Llama Stack's\neval provider backs onto.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the evaluation service: an API for launching an evaluation of a model\n  served on the platform against a selected benchmark suite, tracking run\n  status, and retrieving results.\n- Execute evaluations through lm-evaluation-harness-based jobs, reusing the\n  existing LMEvalJob runner capabilities where they fit.\n- Support custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) through\n  the same launch flow as standard suites.\n- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the\n  evaluated model's version, in the canonical result schema, including the\n  link to the evaluated model version.\n- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the same\n  result record for capacity planning.\n- Expose the API surface that the Llama Stack eval provider integration backs\n  onto.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform against a\n  selected benchmark suite through the evaluation service API, and the run\n  executes and reports status.\n- Custom evaluation tasks with user-defined datasets and metrics run through\n  the same flow as standard suites.\n- On completion, results are persisted to Model Registry custom properties on\n  the evaluated model version, conforming to the canonical result schema.\n- Each evaluation run records tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU time in the\n  result record.\n- The service exposes the API surface required to back Llama Stack's eval\n  provider.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the\n  platform against a selected benchmark suite.\n- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks and run them through\n  the same flow.\n- HLR-8 (P2): evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata for capacity\n  planning (same result record and persistence surface as HLR-3 — bundled, not\n  split).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51736,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab93c870253e5ee8","agent_id":"a1f24615f07c0d279","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"d0ccbf9f-c511-4cc0-9ecb-a2e3f2dbcda7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:15:31.839Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002"}
