{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5729bc645fb1ce","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Evaluation execution engine architecture'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Evaluation execution engine architecture\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's first open question: does the\n30\tplatform evaluation capability build on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview,\n31\talready wrapping EleutherAI lm-evaluation-harness) as the single execution\n32\tpath, or is a new evaluation service needed that can also serve Llama Stack's\n33\teval provider API? The deliverable is a written recommendation, recorded as an\n34\tarchitecture decision, that determines the shape of every downstream\n35\tintegration: what surface the Dashboard reads, what the Data Science Pipelines\n36\tevaluation step calls, and what the Llama Stack eval provider is backed by.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Analyze the LMEvalJob CRD and the TrustyAI service operator: current\n41\t  capabilities, extension points, and limits (multi-suite task selection,\n42\t  custom task definitions, result export, API serving).\n43\t- Analyze Llama Stack's upstream eval provider API contract and what a\n44\t  production eval provider implementation must satisfy.\n45\t- Evaluate whether an LMEvalJob-based path can serve all three consumers\n46\t  (direct launch by users, pipeline steps, Llama Stack eval provider API) or\n47\t  whether a separate evaluation service is required.\n48\t- Produce a recommendation with an architecture decision record, including the\n49\t  criteria used, the risks of each option, and the explicitly enumerated\n50\t  bounded outcomes (extend LMEvalJob vs new evaluation service).\n51\t- Identify any follow-on work the chosen option implies for downstream teams\n52\t  (Dashboard, Pipelines, Llama Stack).\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A recommendation document exists that answers the execution engine question\n57\t  with a single selected option and records the decision rationale.\n58\t- Each option is evaluated against named criteria: ability to launch\n59\t  evaluations against KServe endpoints and Llama Stack distributions, support\n60\t  for standard and custom benchmark tasks, ability to serve the Llama Stack\n61\t  eval provider API, and result persistence hooks.\n62\t- The bounded outcomes are enumerated (extend LMEvalJob as single execution\n63\t  path vs new evaluation service) so the conditional downstream plan can be\n64\t  resolved.\n65\t- Downstream impact on the Dashboard integration, the Data Science Pipelines\n66\t  evaluation step, and the Llama Stack eval provider is stated for the\n67\t  selected option.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0): launching evaluations of served models — gated by this\n72\t  investigation's outcome.\n73\t- HLR-7 (P1): Llama Stack eval provider API backed by the platform evaluation\n74\t  service — gated by this investigation's outcome.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d5379a6620c5ce","agent_id":"a36f2c95917215dda","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"c2326e74-fee8-4027-8f3b-8fc7781dbd72","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:20:28.913Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-be5729bc645fb1ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagen