s customer-fetched) with a citation of the governing\n51\t  license.\n52\t- The classification covers disconnected-environment delivery explicitly.\n53\t- Packaging guidance for the standard suite catalog is stated so the catalog\n54\t  implementation can proceed without further licensing decisions.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box — the\n59\t  delivery mechanism (bundled vs customer-fetched) is gated by this\n60\t  investigation's outcome.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d5379a6620c5ce","agent_id":"a36f2c95917215dda","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"9530dcf4-324a-407a-9e48-9da0b89df8f3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:20:31.251Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-96172b9921364b09","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
