n51\t  Llama Stack distribution) with a selected benchmark suite from the standard\n52\t  catalog.\n53\t- Support custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) through\n54\t  the same launch flow as standard suites.\n55\t- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the\n56\t  evaluated model's version, in the canonical result schema, including the\n57\t  link to the evaluated model version.\n58\t- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the same\n59\t  result record for capacity planning.\n60\t- Preserve existing LMEvalJob behavior for current users of the Tech Preview\n61\t  capability.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform against a\n66\t  selected benchmark suite, and the evaluation executes via the LMEvalJob\n67\t  path.\n68\t- Custom evaluation tasks with user-defined datasets and metrics run through\n69\t  the same flow as standard suites.\n70\t- On completion, results are persisted to Model Registry custom properties on\n71\t  the evaluated model version, conforming to the canonical result schema.\n72\t- Each evaluation run records tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU time in the\n73\t  result record.\n74\t- Existing LMEvalJob usage (pre-extension) continues to function.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the\n79\t  platform against a selected benchmark suite.\n80\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n81\t  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n82\t- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks and run them through\n83\t  the same flow.\n84\t- HLR-8 (P2): evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata for capacity\n85\t  planning (same result record and persistence surface as HLR-3 — bundled, not\n86\t  split).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d5379a6620c5ce","agent_id":"a36f2c95917215dda","session