tthe `fallback_approach` text, so no execution-relevant information is lost.\n126\t\n127\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n128\tSignal fields are type-correct across all 10 epics: E001-E003 carry\n129\t`investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric) with `ai_signals: null`; all\n130\tImplementation epics (E004-E008, both branches) carry `ai_signals` (9-signal\n131\trubric) with `investigation_signals: null`. Every frontmatter value matches\n132\tits rationale table in the corresponding ai-signals file. Values are\n133\tconsistent with content: unresolved gating questions correctly yield\n134\t`open_questions: -1` on E004/E005/E006/E007 and both branches, while E008\n135\t(runs last, everything resolved) correctly gets +1; E007's upstream\n136\tllama-stack coordination yields `external_dependency: -1`; the greenfield\n137\tbranch B is scored conservatively (change_specificity/pattern_precedent/\n138\tadapter_pattern/existing_foundation at or below 0) while the extension branch\n139\tA is scored higher on foundation signals — both justified. Investigation\n140\tsignals are plausible: public sources give `source_accessibility: 1`, legal/\n141\tstakeholder sign-off gives `human_judgment_required: -1`. Computed aggregates\n142\twere not re-derived (pipeline-computed).\n143\t\n144\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n145\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs:\n146\tE008 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review-by-owning-engineers AC;\n147\tE005 has the feature-flag/disabled-by-default AC; branch A preserves existing\n148\tLMEvalJob behavior (backward-compatibility AC for the extension); no konflux\n149\tchain exists, so the build-pipeline AC is N/A. No AC states an external\n150\tschedule constraint (no lab-turnaround or review-cadence soft ACs — the legal\n151\treview dependency on E003 is correctly an edge/AC pair, not a timing AC). No\n152\tepic body references sibling epics by draft ID (grep-verified; references use\n153\t