{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb9ed0c29e55605","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Canonical evaluation result schema'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Canonical evaluation result schema\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's second open question: what is the\n30\tcanonical result format persisted to Model Registry custom properties, and\n31\tdoes it survive benchmark-suite version bumps? The deliverable is a validated\n32\tschema design, prototyped against real MMLU output before commitment, that\n33\tthe evaluation execution path will write and the Dashboard, pipeline gating,\n34\tand comparison views will consume.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Run lm-evaluation-harness against a real MMLU task and capture the actual\n39\t  output structure (per-benchmark scores, aggregation, run metadata).\n40\t- Map that output onto Model Registry custom properties on ModelVersion\n41\t  entities (the documented extension point), respecting property type and size\n42\t  constraints of the Model Registry REST API.\n43\t- Design the canonical result record: per-benchmark scores, the link to the\n44\t  evaluated model version, and cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock,\n45\t  GPU time).\n46\t- Analyze schema resilience to benchmark-suite version bumps (field\n47\t  additions/renames across lm-eval task versions) and specify a\n48\t  versioning/evolution rule.\n49\t- Document the schema and the persistence approach as the committed format.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A schema document defines the canonical evaluation result format persisted\n54\t  to Model Registry custom properties, including per-benchmark scores and\n55\t  cost/duration metadata fields.\n56\t- A prototype persisted real MMLU output to Model Registry custom properties\n57\t  on a model version using the proposed schema.\n58\t- A version-bump analysis demonstrates whether the schema survives\n59\t  benchmark-suite version bumps and states the evolution rule; the prototype\n60\t  is committed only after this validation passes.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-3 (P0): results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version —\n65\t  gated by this investigation's outcome.\n66\t- HLR-8 (P2): cost/duration metadata in the result record — schema designed\n67\t  here.\n68\t- HLR-5 (P1): Dashboard per-benchmark score display and comparison — the\n69\t  rendered fields are defined by this schema.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8623395f67fec7e3","agent_id":"ac4d1cf20445318f5","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"1e395e74-4e39-4815-a1b2-7262164c43a7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:32:23.134Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb9ed0c29e55605","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002"}
