{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab0c6579360e75b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Benchmark dataset redistribution licensing'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Benchmark dataset redistribution licensing\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's third open question: which standard\n30\tbenchmark suites can be redistributed in disconnected environments, and which\n31\tmust be fetched by the customer? The deliverable is a per-suite licensing\n32\tclassification that determines the packaging approach of the standard\n33\tbenchmark suite catalog — bundled with the platform versus documented\n34\tcustomer-side fetch.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Enumerate the candidate standard suites exposed through lm-eval task names\n39\t  (e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag) and the datasets they require.\n40\t- Audit each suite's dataset license for redistribution terms in\n41\t  disconnected/air-gapped delivery.\n42\t- Classify each suite: redistributable (can ship in the platform catalog) vs\n43\t  customer-fetched (documented fetch path required).\n44\t- Record the classification with license citations and the resulting packaging\n45\t  guidance for the standard suite catalog.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Every candidate standard suite has a documented classification\n50\t  (redistributable vs customer-fetched) with a citation of the governing\n51\t  license.\n52\t- The classification covers disconnected-environment delivery explicitly.\n53\t- Packaging guidance for the standard suite catalog is stated so the catalog\n54\t  implementation can proceed without further licensing decisions.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): standard benchmark suites available out of the box — the\n59\t  delivery mechanism (bundled vs customer-fetched) is gated by this\n60\t  investigation's outcome.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8623395f67fec7e3","agent_id":"ac4d1cf20445318f5","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"dfdaf28c-9619-4953-ad18-c2477e8290b2","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:32:24.167Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab0c6579360e75b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002"}
