{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974aef290dfc3800","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Extend LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation recommends a new evaluation service instead\n17\t    of extending LMEvalJob, this epic is replaced by the branch B service epic.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Extend LMEvalJob as the single evaluation execution path\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional plan branch A — applies if the execution engine architecture\n39\tinvestigation recommends building on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob as the single\n40\texecution path. This epic extends the LMEvalJob capability so users can launch\n41\tan evaluation of a model served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama\n42\tStack distribution) against a selected benchmark suite, run custom evaluation\n43\ttasks through the same flow, and have results — including cost/duration\n44\tmetadata — persisted and linked to the Model Registry version of the evaluated\n45\tmodel.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Extend the LMEvalJob-based execution path so an evaluation can be launched\n50\t  against a model served on the platform (KServe InferenceService endpoint or\n51\t  Llama Stack distribution) with a selected benchmark suite from the standard\n52\t  catalog.\n53\t- Support custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) through\n54\t  the same launch flow as standard suites.\n55\t- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the\n56\t  evaluated model's version, in the canonical result schema, including the\n57\t  link to the evaluated model version.\n58\t- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the same\n59\t  result record for capacity planning.\n60\t- Preserve existing LMEvalJob behavior for current users of the Tech Preview\n61\t  capability.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform against a\n66\t  selected benchmark suite, and the evaluation executes via the LMEvalJob\n67\t  path.\n68\t- Custom evaluation tasks with user-defined datasets and metrics run through\n69\t  the same flow as standard suites.\n70\t- On completion, results are persisted to Model Registry custom properties on\n71\t  the evaluated model version, conforming to the canonical result schema.\n72\t- Each evaluation run records tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU time in the\n73\t  result record.\n74\t- Existing LMEvalJob usage (pre-extension) continues to function.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the\n79\t  platform against a selected benchmark suite.\n80\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n81\t  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n82\t- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks and run them through\n83\t  the same flow.\n84\t- HLR-8 (P2): evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata for capacity\n85\t  planning (same result record and persistence surface as HLR-3 — bundled, not\n86\t  split).\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8623395f67fec7e3","agent_id":"ac4d1cf20445318f5","session