{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a14a8c098a6454d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: New evaluation service for execution and the eval provider API\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation recommends building on LMEvalJob as the\n17\t    single execution path instead of a new service, this epic is replaced by the branch\n18\t    A LMEvalJob extension epic.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: -1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 1\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# New evaluation service for execution and the eval provider API\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional plan branch B — applies if the execution engine architecture\n40\tinvestigation recommends a new evaluation service. This epic builds that\n41\tservice under the TrustyAI component (the platform's model-quality component):\n42\tit exposes the platform's evaluation launch surface, executes evaluations of\n43\tmodels served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution)\n44\tagainst selected benchmark suites, supports custom evaluation tasks, persists\n45\tresults — including cost/duration metadata — linked to the Model Registry\n46\tversion of the evaluated model, and serves the API surface that Llama Stack's\n47\teval provider backs onto.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Build the evaluation service: an API for launching an evaluation of a model\n52\t  served on the platform against a selected benchmark suite, tracking run\n53\t  status, and retrieving results.\n54\t- Execute evaluations through lm-evaluation-harness-based jobs, reusing the\n55\t  existing LMEvalJob runner capabilities where they fit.\n56\t- Support custom evaluation tasks (user-defined datasets and metrics) through\n57\t  the same launch flow as standard suites.\n58\t- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the\n59\t  evaluated model's version, in the canonical result schema, including the\n60\t  link to the evaluated model version.\n61\t- Record cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) in the same\n62\t  result record for capacity planning.\n63\t- Expose the API surface that the Llama Stack eval provider integration backs\n64\t  onto.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- A user can launch an evaluation of a model served on the platform against a\n69\t  selected benchmark suite through the evaluation service API, and the run\n70\t  executes and reports status.\n71\t- Custom evaluation tasks with user-defined datasets and metrics run through\n72\t  the same flow as standard suites.\n73\t- On completion, results are persisted to Model Registry custom properties on\n74\t  the evaluated model version, conforming to the canonical result schema.\n75\t- Each evaluation run records tokens, wall-clock time, and GPU time in the\n76\t  result record.\n77\t- The service exposes the API surface required to back Llama Stack's eval\n78\t  provider.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-1 (P0): users can launch an evaluation of a model served on the\n83\t  platform against a selected benchmark suite.\n84\t- HLR-3 (P0): evaluation results are persisted and linked to the Model\n85\t  Registry version of the evaluated model.\n86\t- HLR-4 (P1): users can define custom evaluation tasks and run them through\n87\t  the same flow.\n88\t- HLR-8 (P2): evaluation runs record cost/duration metadata for capacity\n89\t  planning (same result record and persistence surface as HLR-3 — bundled, not\n90\t  split).\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8623395f67fec7e3","agent_id":"ac4d1cf20445318f5","session_id":"544b3ec5-06d3-46ca-8ea6-a4c49a0f57f5","uuid":"f68f8d19-1c4e-4943-9fba-6ce79f078b6a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:32:38.283Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a14a8c098a6454d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002"}
